From 4ad0b96d39dfab39224958571de748195428dfb3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 06:35:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(clarify): bind early answers to the exact displayed
 question [daveey]

tools/clarify_early now builds a question descriptor (ordered displayed
question/choice snapshot + SHA-256 digest + tool call id) and passes it to
providers that declare accepts_question=True. An early answer carrying
decisions ends a blocked clarify only when its binding echoes this tool call
and digest; matching the session alone no longer suffices, so an unrelated
decision recorded in the same session stays in the outbox for normal
delivery. Legacy providers keep the two-argument call; their withdrawals
without decisions (update pause) still end the clarify, their decision
answers are ignored for a bound question.

Tests: tests/tools/test_clarify_early_bound.py (5 of 7 fail on the parent:
missing descriptor, unbound same-session negative control, legacy answer,
foreign tool call); existing early-answer tests now use a bound provider.
